  "result": {
    "summary": "Cache-field math (cached_context_retained, cache_lost, uncached_reconstruction, handoff_packet_tokens, duplicated_evidence, latency_s, effective_handoff_cost) and the routing-candidate effective_handoff_cost addition are correct and match the synthetic acceptance tests. The regression is that format_report's rewrite to a handoffs-only tab table drops previously-visible by_start/recommendations/planner_handoffs sections from the plain-text `orchestrator scorecard --handoffs` output, an unrequested and untested behavior change.",
    "verdict": "request_changes",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/handoff_scorecard.py",
        "line": 382,
        "issue": "format_report(card) previously returned json.dumps(card, indent=1), which included by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs alongside the new handoffs data. This diff replaces it with a tab-separated table that only renders the handoffs rows/medians, silently dropping by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs from the non-JSON (default) CLI text output of `orchestrator scorecard --handoffs`. That data is still returned in --json mode, so the loss is specific to the plain-text path most operators use by default. Nothing in the spec asked to remove or restructure that existing output, and no test (test_cli.py or test_handoff_scorecard.py) checks that by_start/recommendations/planner_handoffs remain visible in text mode, so this out-of-scope regression ships undetected.",
        "severity": "med"
      }
    ],
